```python
def solve(matrix):
    rows = len(matrix)
    cols = len(matrix[0]) if rows > 0 else 0
    for i in range(rows):
        for j in range(cols):
            if matrix[i][j] == 1:
                return (i, j)
    return (-1, -1)
```

